<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hans Kudlich</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1823–1917</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hans Kudlich was a Silesian-born Austrian politician, the youngest deputy in the Austrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reichstag">Reichstag</a> of 1848, whose motion of July that year led to the abolition of the labour services and other obligations of peasants to their landlords. After the revolution's defeat he fled abroad and settled as a doctor in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hans-kudlich.jpg" alt="Hans Kudlich" width="320" height="479" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Eduard Kaiser · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hans_Kudlich.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
